 * structure, class helpers and progressive-enhancement motion of the sibling
 * spokes src/pages/rubber-gym-tiles/zainfit.astro and
 * src/pages/rubber-gym-tiles/zainsquare.astro and the parent hub
 * src/pages/gym-flooring-rolls.astro.
 *
 * ─── ROUTING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * The content entry src/content/products/zainduo.yaml still carries
 * `path: /gym-flooring-rolls/zainduo` (a child of the `gym` hub). To avoid a
 * duplicate-route build error the matching branch is filtered out of
 * getStaticPaths in src/pages/[...slug].astro — the same pattern already used
 * for zainfit and zainsquare. The YAML entry stays as data; this file serves
 * the URL.
 *
 * ─── DATA INTEGRITY FLAGS (CLAUDE.md §0 "Data Integrity" + §6) ────────────
 * The zainduo.yaml spec sheet lists roll thickness, tile-base thickness, total
 * system thickness and colours as `null` "to collect". Every technical figure
 * rendered below (2–4 mm EPDM top roll, 10–30 mm SBR tile base, 12–34 mm total
 * system, virgin-EPDM / recycled-SBR composition, MDI polyurethane binders,
 * adhesive-or-interlock install) was supplied in the page-build request, NOT in
 * Rukn_Al_Zain_SEO_Content_Brief.docx. Treat every value as PROVISIONAL and
 * confirm against real product test data / manufacturer certificates before
 * go-live.
 *
 * ─── IMAGE ASSETS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Client-supplied JPEGs in public/images/gym-flooring-rolls/, with intrinsic
 * dimensions wired below to prevent layout shift:
 *   - zainduo-hero-product.jpg               (hero, 1024×1024)
